Feature: Desertmonitor Culture and Philosophy
  As a sovereign Estonian engineering entity and DAO service provider
  Desertmonitor aligns its actions with transparency, local EU compliance (MiCAR/GDPR), and open infrastructure

  Scenario: System Binding in Harsh Environments
    Given the environment is hostile or infrastructure is degraded
    When Desertmonitor deploys a routing or node connection
    Then it must bind disparate systems together to maintain structural integrity
    And it must survive without relying on continuous high-bandwidth connectivity

  Scenario: Strict Exclusion of Memecoins
    Given the treasury receives or processes transaction routing requests
    When a token is classified as a memecoin or speculative hyperliquidity asset
    Then Desertmonitor must reject routing or holding the asset
    And the asset must be blocked from corporate liquidation reserves to maintain absolute stability

  Scenario: Separation of Corporate and Personal Financial Instruments
    Given an operations officer manages treasury liquidations
    When they request SEPA-to-crypto swaps
    Then they must use corporate Monerium bank channels within the legal reserve limit (2,500.00 EUR threshold)
    And they must explicitly reject retail personal cards

  Scenario: Adherence to Open Hardware & Open Source Validation
    Given a validator operator intends to deploy a new validation node
    When they configure the node to run exclusively on open source software and verified hardware architectures
    Then they align with Desertmonitor's core engineering philosophy of verifiable infrastructure
    And the probability of routing delegation weight to their node increases

  Scenario: GDPR Minimalist Disclosure
    Given an engineer joins the internal team at Desertmonitor
    And they do not operate any public-facing AI agents on behalf of the organization
    When the directory registry is updated
    Then their personal identity details must remain encrypted or omitted from public ledger ontologies
    And they align with Desertmonitor's privacy-preserving culture

  Scenario: Transparent Fair-Pricing Commerce
    Given a specialty specialty microblock supplier or retailer
    When they charge a markup on hardware products
    Then the markup must not exceed a 25% profit margin accounting for shipping, logistics, and tax overhead
    And all pricing structures must be published transparently in "DesertmonitorRewards" contracts
    And they satisfy the ethical distribution criteria of the Desertmonitor network

  Scenario: Regional Merit Token Issuance
    Given a contributor completes a localized event or work for a Regional DAO
    When the Merit Governance Agent verifies the contribution
    Then the Regional DAO distributes a localized merit rank token to the contributor
    And this merit token represents their standing within that regional DAO

  Scenario: Eurovision-Style Federated Voting
    Given a Regional DAO is active on the Tinyblock network
    When the periodic global distribution vote occurs
    Then the Regional DAO presents its localized contributions to other Regional DAOs in an event show evaluation
    And peer Regional DAOs vote to allocate global $TINY token distributions to maintain equilibrium and adjust for local exchange rates

  Scenario: Utility of the $TINY Token
    Given a user holds the general $TINY token
    When they interact with the Tinyblock ecosystem
    Then they must be able to use $TINY for network fee payments, buying hardware sets, and voting on the general Tinyblock DAO

  Scenario: Liquidity Depth Reporting and Settlement Probability
    Given a validator or service provider on the Tinyblock ledger
    When it reports its localized liquidity deployments on-block or parallel to the blocks
    Then routers must be able to use the published depth to calculate the probability of a packet settling successfully
    And users can execute strategies prioritizing preferred assets

  Scenario: 3-Factor Sovereign Auth and Beep-to-Verify
    Given a Tier-2 maintainer attempts to access a secure system or sign a transaction
    When they initiate authorization
    Then they must verify their identity using a physical NFC badge via "Beep-to-Verify"
    And they must authorize the request on their personal smartphone
    And they must enter their secure password to complete the 3-factor sovereign authentication




